# Golden snapshots are byte-exact fixtures. Two of them — handler/request.go
# and bootstrap/bootstrapper.go — are patched copies of the reference template,
# which is CRLF throughout, and preserving those line endings is one of the
# properties the tests assert (a patch that normalises them turns a three-line
# insertion into a diff touching every line).
#
# Without this, git's autocrlf would rewrite the snapshots on checkout and the
# golden tests would fail on one platform and pass on another. The .golden
# extension keeps gofmt away from them; this keeps git away.
internal/scaffold/testdata/golden/*.golden -text -diff
internal/scaffold/testdata/golden/**/*.golden -text -diff

# Everything else is normal text.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.go text eol=lf
*.tmpl text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
